# Cloudflare Pages merges headers of ALL matching rules (no override), so
# multiple Cache-Control rules for the same asset produce duplicate max-age
# values with undefined browser behavior. Keep ONE simple rule for everything:
# HTML (deploys auto-propagate within 5 min) and hashed assets (content-hash
# URLs make long caching unnecessary — a new hash is a new URL).
# Edge TTL is enforced at 300s by the Cloudflare Cache Rule "wanlian911 HTML
# edge cache"; the Browser side revalidates via must-revalidate after 300s.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
